## Borrowed code

No third-party source was copied into this repository. Every contract and
test file in `src/`, `test/` and `script/` was written for this project.

The test-only `MockToken` in `test/mocks/MockToken.sol` is a deliberately
minimal ERC-20 written for this repository. It is not copied from
OpenZeppelin or anywhere else. It exists to model tUSD8's six decimals
exactly, because the real token uses six and a mock with eighteen would
hide a whole class of bug.

Where a pattern follows a well-known idiom — for example `check`/`approve`
separating a read-only decision from the state-changing action, or
`SafeERC20` for token calls — the dependency is imported and credited above
rather than reimplemented.

